      "title": "Setup and model downloads",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## CorridorKey MLX auto-chroma key\n\n1. Install the separately licensed [CorridorKey MLX runtime](https://github.com/nikopueringer/corridorkey-mlx) in ComfyUI's Python environment.\n2. Review the [official CorridorKey model page](https://huggingface.co/nikopueringer/CorridorKey_v1.0).\n3. Download `corridorkey_mlx.safetensors` from the [official v1.0.0 MLX release](https://github.com/nikopueringer/corridorkey-mlx/releases/tag/v1.0.0).\n4. Put the checkpoint in `ComfyUI/models/corridorkey/` or a shared `corridorkey` model folder.\n5. Select green-screen footage in **Load Image**. The selector is intentionally empty in this portable workflow.\n6. Queue the workflow. The checkerboard preview is connected.\n\nCorridorKey uses a separate non-Apache license. Review the [CorridorKey license](https://github.com/nikopueringer/CorridorKey/blob/main/LICENSE) before use. For SAM, Florence, or Impact Pack masks, connect their standard `MASK` output through **CorridorKey Mask Refine** instead of Auto Chroma Hint."
      ],
